  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 212 AM MDT TUE SEP 8 2026\nFriday looks sunny, windy, and cooler behind Thursday night's \ncold front, but Saturday looks warmer again as upper flow backs \nto southwesterly. The southwest flow will be ahead of a deep, \ncold upper low moving southward from the BC coast to just off \nthe WA and OR coast. That low is forecast to move rapidly inland\nacross OR Saturday with a strong surface cold front, gusty winds\nat least 30 mph (partly due to the speed of the incoming low), \nand a chance of showers and thunderstorms, then much cooler \nSunday. Monday will already be warming and drying again as the \nupper low moves all the way to North Dakota, and Tuesday looks \nsunny and warmer still under building high pressure aloft over \nthe Great Basin.",
